The requirement says "the project owner records measured limits". The record Rd3.1a is who_decides: project owner. A small config file readable by tool and human seems best: single source, exact, diffable, and can carry source/date. But the brief explicitly lists candidates: a section of AGENTS.md, a small config file, or the tool's constants. My answer: a small config file (e.g. `project-memory/limits.yaml` or repo-root `.memory-index-limits`), because it's machine-readable for the tool, diffable/versioned so a reviewer sees when the interim stops, and separate from the shared tool; AGENTS.md remains the human instruction and points to it. Include fields: per agent: name, start file(s), max_lines, max_bytes (with unit stated: bytes vs UTF-16 code units; agy tokens), where measured (command/date), and an `interim: true` marker while any row is the example. Tool computes the strictest among listed agents, with unit normalization (lines, bytes, code units) — careful: comparing 24,000 bytes to 25,000 UTF-16 code units is not apples to apples for non-ASCII; the tool can measure INDEX.md in bytes and in UTF-16 code units. That's a real design point.

