Wording: "the strictest start-file limit among the agents whose session start loads INDEX.md." who_decides: project owner (which agents those are, and so the strictest limit). Rd3.1a "work on the project" → change. Also C's file rows should be only those agents; this ties C and D: the config lists session-start readers, not all agents.

Cost/risk: an agent that works but doesn't read INDEX at start may later read it mid-session where a limit still applies (context budget), but that is the agent's own budget, not the start-file limit; the narrower set can let INDEX grow past an agent that reads it on demand. If the owner routes all agents to read it at start, set is all agents anyway.

