**D.** The readers at session start, not all who work. Wording: group title already right ("every agent that reads it"), prose says "agents that read it"; change Rd3.1a to "among the agents whose session start loads `INDEX.md`". Why: a start-file limit is a property of the load path, not of working on the project; an agent that never loads INDEX at start places no limit on it. An agent that reads it on demand is bound by context budget but not this start-file limit; if the owner routes it to read INDEX at start (AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md say so), it joins the set. who_decides stays the project owner (which agents, and so the strictest limit) — the record's who_decides must name "which agents load INDEX.md at session start" rather than "work on the project".

